## 2. Scroll Animation Libraries

### Intersection Observer API (Native)
**Purpose**: Detect when elements enter/leave viewport
**No Installation Required**: Built into modern browsers
**Use Cases**: Lazy loading, scroll-triggered reveals, performance monitoring

```tsx
const useInView = () => {
  const ref = useRef(null);
  const [isInView, setIsInView] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(([entry]) => {
      setIsInView(entry.isIntersecting);
    });
    observer.observe(ref.current);
    return () => observer.disconnect();
  }, []);

  return [ref, isInView];
};
```

### AOS (Animate On Scroll)
**Purpose**: Lightweight scroll animation library
**Installation**: `npm install aos`
**Best For**: Simple fade-ins, slides, and basic scroll effects
**Limitation**: Less flexible than Framer Motion for complex interactions

### Lenis (Smooth Scroll)
**Purpose**: Smooth scrolling experience
**Installation**: `npm install @studio-freight/lenis`
**Features**: Momentum scrolling, scroll hijacking prevention, performance optimized

